# =============================================================================
# .gitignore — Alpemix ALV Converter AI Spec-Kit
# =============================================================================

# --- Build Artifacts ---
*.dcu
*.dcp
*.bpl
*.exe
*.pyc
*.pyo
__pycache__/
*.spec.bak

# --- IDE Temporary / Generated Files ---
*.identcache
*.local
*.stat
*.tvsconfig
__history/
__recovery/
.idea/
.vscode/

# --- Build / Output Directories ---
build/
dist/
output/

# --- Dependencies and Caches ---
node_modules/
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
modules/

# --- Sensitive / Credential Files ---
*.key
*.pfx
*.p12
.env
.env.*

# --- Large / Noisy Files ---
*.log
*.dmp
*.bak
*.tmp

# --- OS Artifacts ---
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
analysis/
.serena

# --- Generated skill links (never committed) ---
# tools/generate-ai-configs.ps1 creates one junction/symlink per .agents/skills/*
# here, because Claude Code only discovers skills under .claude/skills/. These
# are machine-local links, regenerated by the script on any clone. They must NOT
# be committed: git does not store a junction — it would follow it and commit a
# full second copy of every skill, which is exactly the duplicate source of
# truth this whole scheme exists to prevent.
.claude/skills/

# --- Working staging area ---
# The converter's own Delphi and Python sources under src/ ARE repo content —
# this repo publishes their built binaries, so the source that produced them
# is visible too. What stays out is everything that is generated or huge:
#
#   src/temp/   Delphi .dcu output, PyInstaller's work directory, build venv
#
# src/bin/ IS committed, deliberately: the release archive ships in the repo as
# well as on the releases page, so a clone carries the runnable build without a
# separate download. The cost is real and was accepted — 53 MB in every clone,
# permanently, and the same bytes stored twice.
#
# A real .alv recording is proprietary and never belongs in git either; the
# staging rules are in .agents/rules/input-resolution.md.
src/temp/
*.alv

# --- Image variant sets kept locally, not shipped ---
docs/images/*/
